1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,420
The pressure built in the morning, after the club established a new condition for the season: every athlete would give two hours a week to the open class.

2
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:14,750
“In this shop we do not pay for good health,” the manager said.

3
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:26,969
“We build it.” The food in the canteen changed, the drug cabinet was locked, and the defense of the old timetable finally collapsed.

4
00:00:26,969 --> 00:00:39,443
The worry was the bird in the hand: a pledge to play in the spring, a meal plan that attracted nobody, and an ideal diet written by somebody who had never been hungry.

5
00:00:39,443 --> 00:00:46,187
The suggestion of a bath and a basin of warm water produced a relief that no formula could.

6
00:00:46,187 --> 00:00:55,906
Immigration, infection, and consumption were the three old words on the wall, and nobody in the century had liked them.

7
00:00:55,906 --> 00:00:59,146
The symptom that mattered was silence.

8
00:00:59,146 --> 00:01:05,185
“A constitutional weakness is not a personal failure,” the doctor said.

9
00:01:05,185 --> 00:01:20,009
“But an addiction to busyness is a complication of the modern timetable.” The rhythm of the week, the outlook of the committee, and the humor of the physiotherapist all had to change together.

10
00:01:20,009 --> 00:01:24,678
“You can relieve distress without torture,” she said.

11
00:01:24,678 --> 00:01:43,226
“Scissors, a satellite image, and a disciplined hour of sleep will do more than an invasion of advice.” The irrigation of the pitch, the ash in the basin, and the hearty soup were small mercies, and the team counted them.

12
00:01:43,226 --> 00:01:47,116
The pressure did not come only from management.

13
00:01:47,116 --> 00:01:57,005
A fixation on numbers, an adaptation of the whole club, and the physiology of digestion were now part of the programme.

14
00:01:57,005 --> 00:02:00,659
“We are able to help,” Maya wrote.

15
00:02:00,659 --> 00:02:12,738
“We are not able to hurry a body through a century in one season.” The window of the sports center stayed open all winter, and the movement of the class went on.

16
00:02:12,738 --> 00:02:18,913
There was no peace in the canteen, and the opposition to the new rule was loud.

17
00:02:18,913 --> 00:02:42,076
“The cost is real,” the manager said, “and the way we thank the volunteers is by counting them.” An indication of diabetes in one player, a bank of tests, and a family history of illness made the argument concrete; the word “bank” came back, and this time nobody laughed at it.
